From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:59:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: Keep absent SS receivers quiet on USB2 links

The USB mux state also brings up the SS PHY for USB2-only devices and
cables. A bounded handover retrain which finds no SS receiver is normal
there. Keep that ENOTCONN result in the helper's debug trace and reserve
the PHY warning for control and reset errors.

The return value still describes successful port-power restoration; no
reset, retry, ownership or lane configuration behavior changes.

Fixes: 8df6578502e7
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 579de97d141f1fbcaca250b7d17258da2988ce9b)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index e831e597fd..dbc5365ff5 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -4569,7 +4569,8 @@ static int atcphy_usb3_port_on(struct apple_atcphy *atcphy, struct atcphy_usb3_p
 	else if (!ret && atcphy->fixed_usb2 && atcphy->hw->has_t8140_dp) {
 		int retrain = usb_hub_port_retrain(pm->root, 1);
 
-		if (retrain < 0)
+		/* An absent SS receiver is normal for a USB2-only device or cable. */
+		if (retrain < 0 && retrain != -ENOTCONN)
 			dev_warn(atcphy->dev, "SuperSpeed handover retrain failed: %d\n", retrain);
 		/* Power was restored even if no receiver answered the bounded retrain. */
 	}
